# What the source distribution (the release `.tar.gz`) ships.
#
# setuptools-scm replaces setuptools' default sdist file list with "every file git
# tracks", so without this the tarball carried 4.2 MB of design PNGs: assets/promo.png
# (the README banner) and assets/source/*.png (the artwork build_assets.py renders from).
# Those are build-time *inputs*. The two files anything actually loads at runtime --
# tintaview/assets/generated/{logo_full.png,tintaview.ico} -- are committed inside the
# package and shipped via [tool.setuptools.package-data], which MANIFEST.in does not
# govern, so pruning here cannot reach them: the wheel came out byte-identical (77
# entries, same CRCs) while the sdist went from 4.70 MB to 0.59 MB.
#
# Nothing on any install or update path reads the sdist. install.sh, install.ps1 and
# `tintaview update` all fetch the wheel from the GitHub Release, and the wheel is
# py3-none-any, so pip prefers it everywhere. The tarball exists only so the wheel can be
# rebuilt from source, and that needs none of the files below.
prune assets

# Pruned *for coherence, not for size* -- together these are 48 KB. scripts/build_assets.py
# renders from assets/source/, and tests/test_assets.py loads that script to exercise its
# --check. Leave either in and the tarball ships a script and a test that cannot run:
# both fail with FileNotFoundError once the artwork above is gone (verified). The cost is
# that the suite can no longer be run from an unpacked sdist, which matters to distro
# packagers and to nobody else; CI runs it from the git checkout, which this file does
# not affect.
prune scripts
prune tests
